{
  "title": "Eliminate ambiguous Core Data entities in iOS tests",
  "description": "The iOS unit suite creates many independent \
`NSPersistentContainer(name: \"Ramekin\")` instances from the bundled model. \
Core Data then logs that `CachedRecipe` and `ShoppingItem` fail to find a \
unique entity match for their generated managed-object subclasses. In PR #652 \
this made a test insertion through `ShoppingItem(context:)` unreliable once \
other containers had loaded, even though the same code worked in isolation.\n\
\n\
Create a shared in-memory Core Data test factory that avoids registering \
competing models or inserts entities through the target context's model. \
Migrate the existing recipe-cache, shopping-mutation, shopping-sync, and \
shopping-store tests to it, then assert the suite runs without \
ambiguous-entity diagnostics.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "tests",
    "core-data",
  ],
